[h1]Entertaining Ideas[/h1]
[b]36 new recreation buildings, one for nearly every rung of the tech ladder[/b], so a colony always has something worth doing - whether it is chewing pemmican in a hide tent or running an archotech lounge.

[list]
[*]RimWorld [b]1.5 and 1.6[/b]
[*][b]No new research.[/b] Everything gates on projects the game already has.
[*][b]No Harmony, no dependencies.[/b] Safe to add to an existing save.
[*]Things [b]animate while they are being used[/b] - pinball balls fly, arcade screens play, fish swim, sacks arc through the air.
[/list]

[hr]
[h2]Tribal and medieval - no power, no research[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Knucklebone mat[/b] - the thinking game a tribe can build on day one.
[*][b]Seed pit board[/b] - mancala, carved for a tribe. No chairs? They sit on the ground.
[*][b]Storyteller's stump[/b] - one colonist stands on it beside a campfire and tells a story; the rest gather round, and the story takes shape in the smoke: a thrumbo, a raider, a ship, a mechanoid. A good talker has the fire hanging on every word. A bad one goes on a bit.
[*][b]Shadow lantern theater[/b] - a lamp, a linen screen and a drum the flame turns by itself. A crowd of six can watch.
[*][b]Soaking tub[/b] - a wood-fired barrel colonists climb [i]into[/i]. Warms the room, steams while lit, and needs a bucket of water carried out between soaks.
[*][b]Hammock[/b] - rest that is not a bed. Needs a wall or a column at each end to hang from.
[*][b]Skittles lane[/b] - nine pins that stay where the ball leaves them until somebody walks down and stands them back up.
[*][b]Cornhole[/b] - one board, a throwing line, two players taking turns in their own colours.
[*][b]Lawn noughts and crosses[/b] - a rope grid pegged out on the grass, played by throwing bean bags into the squares.
[*][b]Jigsaw table[/b] - a puzzle that stays where it was left. Anyone who pulls up a chair adds pieces, over several sittings. Finish it and everyone who helped is pleased with themselves - then frame it and hang it on a wall.
[*][b]Board game table[/b] - a cupboard of five games. The first to sit down picks one: [i]Colonists of the Rim, Raid!, Orbital Trader, Caravan Routes[/i] or [i]Muffalo & Thrumbo[/i]. Up to four players.
[*][b]Table tennis[/b] - one player at each end, or practise alone against the far end.
[*][b]Giant four-in-a-row[/b] - an upright frame for two. Face it towards where the players will stand.
[*][b]Tangle mat[/b] - up to three colonists, a spinner, and somebody always falls over.
[*][b]Armillary sphere[/b] - brass rings turning on their own clockwork. It does nothing. It is beautiful.
[/list]

[h2]Industrial[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Four pinball tables[/b] - classic, Boomalope Blitz, Mech Rampage and the Archotech Dreamtable, each with a painted backglass and score reels that climb while somebody plays. (The Dreamtable needs spacer research.)
[*][b]Two cocktail arcade tables[/b] - [i]ORE RUSH[/i], a mining maze, and [i]THRUMBO![/i], a scaffold climb with rocks rolling down at you. Two seats each, a title screen when idle, and real chip-tune bleeps.
[*][b]Karaoke machine[/b] - the singer always has fun. Everyone else decides for themselves, based on the singer's skill and whether they like them. Being well liked covers for being terrible.
[*][b]Swimming pool[/b] - painted as terrain in [i]any shape you like[/i]. The filter claims every tile joined to it, and water, power and evaporation all scale with what you drew.
[*][b]Aquarium[/b] - fish that actually swim, not a flipbook.
[*][b]Air hockey[/b] - a hissing table, a puck that banks off the rails, a mallet at each end.
[*][b]Massage chair, heated tub, bowling lane[/b] and [b]two orreries[/b] - a tabletop model and a grand one under glass, both clockwork.
[/list]

[h2]Spacer and ultra[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Vista panels[/b] - 1, 2 or 3 tiles wide, set into the wall so nothing in front of them is disturbed. They show dawn, daylight, sunset and stars on the local clock, light the room to match, and ease cabin fever in a sealed base.
[*][b]Hologame pod[/b] - a board of light that tunes itself just past your ability.
[*][b]Dreamloop holotheater[/b] - aim it at a wall and the wall becomes the screen. A whole room can watch.
[*][b]Gravball court[/b] - 3x3, up to four players, the ball held in a lazy orbit.
[/list]

[hr]
[h2]Good to know[/h2]
[list]
[*]Electric games and screens can [b]break down[/b] like a television, and need a component to repair.
[*]Anything that needs looking after - a tub to fill, pins to set up, a finished jigsaw to frame - is picked up as ordinary work.
[*]Chairs matter: the jigsaw and board game tables seat as many players as there are chairs pulled up to their sides.
[*]The storyteller's stump needs a lit campfire (or any modded fire pit) within six tiles.
[*]Every build shows its version number in the mod list. [b]If you report a bug, please include it.[/b]
[/list]

[h2]Compatibility[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Dubs Bad Hygiene[/b] - optional. Tubs and the aquarium can be plumbed in, and a soak washes the colonist.
[*][b]Vanilla Furniture Expanded[/b] - optional. The comfort furniture moves onto VFE's own research, so nothing here arrives earlier than VFE's equivalents.
[*]Load order does not matter.
[/list]

[h2]Not yet[/h2]
Colonists cannot be posed without Harmony, so the motion happens on the buildings rather than the people. Only the arcade tables have sound so far.
